  "_notes": {
    "ING": "id: [name, category, pack, rule (key in RULES)]; prices live in prices.json",
    "RECIPES": "your real recipes only; batch:true = reheats well (add keeps); macros are estimates per standard portion",
    "ATTR": "what each ingredient is, for eating-style filters",
    "STORES": "carries: the aisles (ING categories) a store stocks; omit it for a full grocery store",
    "COOK": "how much one pack is in cooking units: [amount, unit]",
    "CONV": "extra units per pack, so recipes can be written in kitchen units; approximate (1 medium onion is about 1 cup diced). Volume (tsp, tbsp, cup) and weight (oz, lb) convert within their family",
    "FLAGS": "cautions shown wherever an ingredient appears; ING_FLAGS lists them per ingredient. Flagged items can be tracked, priced and bought, and always show their flag. cls is the chip style (default r-flag, amber); r-alert (red) is for Dirty Dozen items bought conventional",
    "items": "recipes with items are written as cooked: qty and unit for the whole recipe, which makes serves standard portions. pantry:true items are assumed on hand and never priced."
  },
